{"name":"Arrow Creek","hex":"#927257","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arrow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A projectile consisting of a shaft, a point and a tail with stabilizing fins that is shot from a bow.","A sign or symbol used to indicate a direction (e.g.→)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move swiftly and directly (like an arrow).","To let fly swiftly and directly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrow"},{"term":"creek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small inlet, often saltwater, leading to the sea or to the main channel of a river, especially a river estuary.","The inner part of a port that is used as a dock for small boats."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arrow Creek (Fresno County, California)","blocks":[{"text":"Arrow Creek is a stream in Kings Canyon National Park in Fresno County, California, United States. It is a tributary of the South Fork Kings River."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow_Creek_(Fresno_County%2C_California)","wikidata":"Q4796120"},{"title":"Arrow Creek (Fergus County, Montana)","blocks":[{"text":"Arrow Creek is a tributary of the Missouri River in Montana in the United States. Approximately 45 miles (73 km) long, it rises in the Lewis and Clark National Forest near Highwood Baldy in the Highwood Mountains in southern Chouteau County. It flows south then east, then northeast and joins the Missouri in the White Cliffs Area on the border between Chouteau and Fergus counties."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow_Creek_(Fergus_County%2C_Montana)","wikidata":"Q4069890"},{"title":"Arrow","blocks":[{"text":"An arrow is a fin-stabilized projectile launched by a bow. A typical arrow usually consists of a long, stiff, straight shaft with a weighty arrowhead attached to the front end, multiple fin-like stabilizers called fletchings mounted near the rear, and a slot at the rear end called a nock f